    "# Philippines Earthquake: Damage Proxy Maps, Nov 2023 The **Earth Observatory of Singapore – Remote Sensing Lab (EOS-RS)** produced these damage proxy maps for Philippines Earthquake (Nov 2023) from synthetic aperture radar (SAR) satellite images. Each map is a separate ZIP below with its GeoTIFF, a KMZ for Google Earth, the PNG figures and a text file describing how it was made and how to read it. ## Maps in this dataset - **EOS-RS Damage Proxy Map: Philippines, Earthquake, 23 Nov 2023, v0.9 wbd** (superseded) - **EOS-RS Damage Proxy Map: Philippines, Earthquake, 23 Nov 2023, v0.9 wbd** (superseded) - **EOS-RS Damage Proxy Map: Philippines, Earthquake, 23 Nov 2023, v0.9** - **EOS-RS Damage Proxy Map: Philippines, Earthquake, 23 Nov 2023, v0.9** - **EOS-RS Damage Proxy Map: Philippines, Earthquake, 23 Nov 2023, v0.5 wbd** (superseded) - **EOS-RS Damage Proxy Map: Philippines, Earthquake, 23 Nov 2023, v0.5 ** (superseded) - **EOS-RS Damage Proxy Map: Philippines, Earthquake, 23 Nov 2023, v0.5 ** (superseded) **More map details and files:** **More map details and files:** **Credits:** Earth Observatory of Singapore - Remote Sensing Lab (EOS-RS), Contains modified Copernicus Sentinel data (2023)"
